      "side": 1,
      "message": "[warning] Line 126: 🟡 `Lrc::connectivityChanged()` now always triggers both `connectivityChanged()` and `networkInterfaceChanged()`. That means every generic connectivity event is treated as an interface-change event, which may cause unnecessary call migration/reconfiguration churn. Gate `networkInterfaceChanged()` behind an actual interface-change signal/state check if available.",
      "revId": "6954ea94f64546d7b77a13bc297b2c1fa962f90c",
      "serverId": "1e26b4c1-6b8c-47ff-9df7-501b633d3b5a"
